  "Question": "The symbol \\(25_b\\) represents a two-digit number in the base \\(b.\\) If the number \\(52_b\\) is double the number \\(25_b,\\) then \\(b\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(7\\)",
    "B": "\\(8\\)",
    "C": "\\(9\\)",
    "D": "\\(11\\)",
    "E": "\\(12\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "In base \\(b\\), the left digit of a two-digit numeral counts groups of \\(b\\). Hence\n\\[\n25_b=2b+5,\n\\qquad 52_b=5b+2.\n\\]\nThe base must be an integer greater than \\(5\\), so that every displayed digit is allowed.\n\nUsing the doubling condition,\n\\[\n5b+2=2(2b+5)=4b+10,\n\\]\nwhich gives \\(b=8\\). This is a valid base; indeed, \\(25_8=21\\) and \\(52_8=42\\). Therefore \\(b=8\\), choice B.",
